# Kernel build #16 (k16): the .config difference from build #15 (k15), as a Kconfig fragment.
#
# k16 = k15-nouveau + 0112 (gb_vnni: escape the task name; no config change) + 0113 (gki_defconfig + BUILD.bazel: the
# Realtek SD-card reader drivers as modules). The full .config of k16 is k15's plus exactly these five lines
# (diff of the two build outputs kernel_x86_64_dot_config, 2026-10-31; acceptance check K-02 in K16.md):
#   k15 .config sha256 34195d3a91d497da89b2a71c55e3288b8c2a9de975a45adfe71c62c377df8a0e
#   k16 .config sha256 b4a0a55850256bcb78940d061036632f7494022d9da4df48a521ada8410429f7
# 0113 sets the four driver symbols in arch/x86/configs/gki_defconfig at the place `make savedefconfig` puts them;
# Kconfig adds CONFIG_MISC_RTSX itself (selected by the two MISC drivers). Unchanged and needed: CONFIG_MFD_CORE=m
# (lapis's own first-stage mfd-core.ko is what the drivers link against), CONFIG_MMC=y, CONFIG_MMC_BLOCK=y,
# CONFIG_USB_STORAGE=y and CONFIG_USB_UAS=y (a mass-storage-class reader needs nothing new).
# Use 0113 to build k16; this file documents what it changes. The four modules (rtsx_usb, rtsx_usb_sdmmc, rtsx_pci,
# rtsx_pci_sdmmc) are loaded only by modalias in the native image (/odm/lib/modules/modules.alias, modules.dep).
CONFIG_MISC_RTSX=m
CONFIG_MISC_RTSX_PCI=m
CONFIG_MISC_RTSX_USB=m
CONFIG_MMC_REALTEK_PCI=m
CONFIG_MMC_REALTEK_USB=m
